Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

cavekit-certificate-trust.md R4 / T-534. retryDueToTLSIntolerance remembered ANY handshake error not on its
short exclusion list as intolerance at the connection's maximum version and retried one version lower. With
TLS 1.3 on (security.tls.version.max 4) that turns every certificate-verification failure against a TLS 1.3
server into a second attempt at TLS 1.2, which trips the server's downgrade sentinel (RFC 8446 §4.1.3), so
NSS reports SSL_ERROR_RX_MALFORMED_SERVER_HELLO — and the user reads "malformed Server Hello" for a revoked
certificate (ssl.com's and DigiCert's revoked demo hosts, measured 2026-10-25; the same hosts at a TLS 1.2
cap say SEC_ERROR_REVOKED_CERTIFICATE; badssl.com, a TLS 1.2 server, never showed it). The retried socket
also carries no certificate verdict (nsITransportSecurityInfo.errorCode 0), so an embedder cannot recover
the real error either. Now a SEC_ERROR_* / mozilla::pkix / SSL_ERROR_BAD_CERT_DOMAIN failure is never a
reason to retry lower.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 security/manager/ssl/nsNSSIOLayer.cpp | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/security/manager/ssl/nsNSSIOLayer.cpp b/security/manager/ssl/nsNSSIOLayer.cpp
index a0ebf31146..3fb647b45d 100644
--- a/security/manager/ssl/nsNSSIOLayer.cpp
+++ b/security/manager/ssl/nsNSSIOLayer.cpp
@@ -1034,6 +1034,19 @@ retryDueToTLSIntolerance(PRErrorCode err, nsNSSSocketInfo* socketInfo)
   // be used to conclude server is TLS intolerant.
   // Note this only happens during the initial SSL handshake.
 
+  // A certificate-verification failure is the server's CERTIFICATE, not its TLS
+  // version, so it must not be remembered as intolerance: against a TLS 1.3
+  // server the retry at TLS 1.2 trips the server's downgrade sentinel and NSS
+  // reports SSL_ERROR_RX_MALFORMED_SERVER_HELLO, which buries the real error
+  // (a revoked certificate shown as "malformed Server Hello"; measured on
+  // ssl.com's and DigiCert's revoked demo hosts, 2026-10-25). The same error at
+  // TLS 1.2, with no retry possible, reports SEC_ERROR_REVOKED_CERTIFICATE.
+  if ((err >= SEC_ERROR_BASE && err < SEC_ERROR_LIMIT) ||
+      (err >= mozilla::pkix::ERROR_BASE && err < mozilla::pkix::END_OF_LIST) ||
+      err == SSL_ERROR_BAD_CERT_DOMAIN) {
+    return false;
+  }
+
   SSLVersionRange range = socketInfo->GetTLSVersionRange();
   nsSSLIOLayerHelpers& helpers = socketInfo->SharedState().IOLayerHelpers();
 
